<title>FINLAND: Cheaper paper depressed Finnish export prices - SF.</title>
<headline>Cheaper paper depressed Finnish export prices - SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fall in Finnish September export prices was mainly due to cheaper pulp, paper and base metals, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>SF earlier said export prices fell 0.5 percent in September from August, and were down 3.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>&quot;Export prices have now fallen steadily since April this year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Import prices rose 0.5 percent in September on August, and were up 2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
